# {{ package_name }}

Generated CrateStack TypeScript client package (`swr` preset — issue #304). One file per model
under `src/models/`, holding that model's types **and** plain, framework-free `async` functions —
no client class, no React import. Import exactly the functions you call.

```ts
import { CratestackRuntime } from "{{ package_name }}";
{% if models %}
import { {{ models[0].get_fn }}, {{ models[0].list_fn }} } from "{{ package_name }}/models/{{ models[0].file_stem }}";
{% endif %}

const runtime = new CratestackRuntime("https://api.example.com", {
  basePath: "{{ base_path }}",
});
```

Every function takes the runtime as its first argument, so it's callable from a React component, a
server action, a plain Node script, or a test — the same shape everywhere, with no hook required.

